WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.210
Ari reads a headline:

2
00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.882
Tesla says its new Roadster can fly.

3
00:00:04.972 --> 00:00:08.502
He pictures lifting off over the traffic jam
on his way to work.

4
00:00:08.502 --> 00:00:10.741
But what is actually being claimed?

5
00:00:10.931 --> 00:00:12.651
This car is our illustration,

6
00:00:12.651 --> 00:00:15.371
not Tesla’s car or its demonstration.

7
00:00:15.371 --> 00:00:18.429
Let’s follow the claim, one step at a time.

8
00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:21.109
Tesla’s Roadster page lists three versions:

9
00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:23.642
Performance, Thrust and Rocket.

10
00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:25.912
It says all three use a fan system

11
00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:28.242
that pulls air out from beneath the car.

12
00:00:28.242 --> 00:00:32.292
That suction presses the car
down onto the road, for grip.

13
00:00:32.292 --> 00:00:34.122
So the fans hold the car down.

14
00:00:34.122 --> 00:00:35.622
They aren’t what lifts it.

15
00:00:35.812 --> 00:00:37.332
For that, Thrust and Rocket add

16
00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:40.135
what Tesla calls cold-gas thrusters.

17
00:00:40.225 --> 00:00:41.825
Here’s the basic idea.

18
00:00:41.825 --> 00:00:45.025
Gas stored under pressure
rushes out through a nozzle.

19
00:00:45.025 --> 00:00:48.485
Pushing gas one way
pushes the thruster the other way.

20
00:00:48.485 --> 00:00:50.635
That push is called thrust.

21
00:00:50.725 --> 00:00:55.525
A NASA report on small spacecraft
describes cold-gas thrusters this way.

22
00:00:55.525 --> 00:00:57.335
That explains the principle,

23
00:00:57.335 --> 00:01:00.295
not Tesla’s design,
or whether it’s safe.

24
00:01:00.485 --> 00:01:04.270
On Rocket, Tesla says thrusters
around the edge of the car

25
00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:08.125
support forward and upward acceleration,
and turning.

26
00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:10.292
Then it adds:
so yes, it can fly.

27
00:01:10.382 --> 00:01:11.692
That is Tesla’s claim.

28
00:01:11.692 --> 00:01:12.832
We haven’t tested it,

29
00:01:12.832 --> 00:01:15.201
and no independent check is shown here.

30
00:01:15.391 --> 00:01:16.751
Now the fine print.

31
00:01:16.751 --> 00:01:20.631
Tesla lists Rocket as invite only,
with seating for one,

32
00:01:20.631 --> 00:01:23.401
and says it isn’t available
in all regions.

33
00:01:23.491 --> 00:01:25.051
And the page carries a note:

34
00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.529
not approved for public road use.

35
00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:31.726
So a flying commute over traffic
is not what this page offers.

36
00:01:31.916 --> 00:01:34.876
A headline like this blends
three different questions.

37
00:01:34.876 --> 00:01:37.076
What did the maker claim, or show?

38
00:01:37.076 --> 00:01:38.616
Who can actually get one?

39
00:01:38.616 --> 00:01:40.606
And is it approved for the road?

40
00:01:40.896 --> 00:01:44.449
"It can fly" is where the questions start,
not where they end.
